WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.330
- And all of us will stop at
nothing to drive you happy.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.060
- [Advertiser] We'll drive
you happy at Carvana.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.710
- [Narrator] You might
recognize these commercials

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.730
for Carvana.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.670
The online car dealer that
delivers cars to your home

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.770
or sends them to one of
their vending machines

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.780
spread across the country.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.620
The company says it wants to
change the way we buy cars.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.190
And in 2021, investors took notice.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.250
It's revenue had more than
doubled from the previous year,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.490
and its stock value
skyrocketed by over 1,000%,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.320
from a low point in 2020.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.180
- I think Carvana is a
perfect example of a stock

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.500
that had everything go right for it

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.170
during the first part of the
pandemic, and subsequently,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.270
seems to have almost
everything going wrong.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.410
- [Narrator] The company share price

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.780
started to fall in late 2021.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.170
Plummeting by 95% over several months.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.660
And the things that had
once driven Carvana's growth

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.300
were now signaling trouble to investors.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.223
So, what went wrong?

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.670
Carvana has never actually posted

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.170
an annual profit,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.720
instead focusing on growth.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.000
- Carvana, put money into hiring.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.670
Into new reconditioning centers,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.100
to fix up the cars that they
buy and sell them again.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.810
Carvana's put a lot of
money into marketing

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.507
including the big Super
Bowl ads and things like.

00:01:12.507 --> 00:01:15.300
- Did I tell you I bought
our car from Carvana.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.950
- But also the car vending machines.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.210
They spend a lot of money,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.680
and they have always spent a lot of money.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.940
And they don't make a lot of money.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.410
- [Narrator] The company grew steadily

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.510
and went public in 2017.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.910
But it was in 2020 amid the pandemic,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.790
when the share price really took off.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.210
In February 2021, CEO, Ernie Garcia,

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:36.120
talked to CNBC about Carvana's growth.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.450
- I think what COVID did is
it shifted psychology faster

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.860
in the direction of trying new things.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.770
And so I do think that
the business probably has

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.760
more demands today than it
would've had absent COVID.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.110
- [Narrator] As demand increased,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.380
three main things were helping
fuel growth for the company.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.320
One was its method for
accounting for car loans.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.290
Like other auto dealers,
Carvana offers customers loans

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.250
to buy their cars,

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.960
and sells the debt to investors,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.990
who buy bonds of the claim
on customer loan payments.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.600
This is a process called securitization.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.120
But unlike others, Carvana
off-loads its loans

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.050
from its balance-sheet,

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.550
to make a gain up front,

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.950
rather than making a gain over time.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.600
Low interest rates at the time

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.390
helped make the loans
appealing to those investors,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.980
who had a higher risk appetite

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.470
and were more comfortable
with consumer credit.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:26.730
In 2021, Carvana made 37% of
the company's gross profit

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.250
from gains on loan sales.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.570
The second thing fueling growth,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.030
was the rising cost of used cars.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.240
A global chip shortage,
restricted production of new cars,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.550
sending up the cost of used ones.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.280
This benefited dealers across the market.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.460
And the third, was its
online low contact model.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.910
Which allowed cars to be
bought and sold across states.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:51.480
- The process that Carvana promises

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.070
is appealing to a lot of people.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.540
You don't have any sales people,

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.770
you know what your price is,

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.480
you know that you have financing going in.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.040
Like it's kind of like, a one click,

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.160
you know you can buy a
car from your living room.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.050
- [Narrator] Carvana's platform was ideal

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.060
for a social distancing world.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.500
And its stock followed the trend

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.660
of other virtually focused companies.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.970
- They were, you know, really
thriving during the pandemic.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.210
Stock was on a steady upward trajectory.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.670
And then the wind changed direction.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.080
- [Narrator] After the peak in August,

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.330
share value started to slip.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.180
Spikes in COVID cases, supply chain issues

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.390
and rising inflation
began to spook investors.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.650
- I think it started with

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.140
kind of a broader growth stock pullback.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.140
They were like other
companies that struggled

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.120
with the pandemic high expectations

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.890
like Peloton and Netflix.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.630
- [Narrator] In February,
the company announced

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.270
that it would acquire
used car auction business,

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.210
Adesa US for 2.2 billion,

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.920
to expand their physical locations

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.620
for inspecting and reconditioning cars.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.410
But in April, the company
announced their first ever decline

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.970
in quarterly sales.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.010
And share value dropped.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.740
- With Carvana, you know
they had this growing demand,

00:03:58.740 --> 00:03:59.850
and they raced to meet this demand.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.140
And they grew, they grew, they grew.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.600
And then all of a sudden, you
know the tide kind of turns.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.490
Demand isn't there for whatever reason,

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.320
or isn't there to the
level that they expected.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.030
And now investors are looking, you know,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.500
kind of at the nitty
gritty of the business,

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.930
'cause it seems like growth
isn't gonna be the story.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.400
- [Narrator] The tailwinds
that had contributed

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.680
to Carvana's growth and boost in stock,

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.020
were now becoming headwinds.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.750
Demand was cooling for
their securitizations.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.290
Fears grew that rising inflation
and a potential recession

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.800
would make it harder for car
buyers to pay back their loans.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.690
Investors' appetite for growth stocks

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.030
and consumer credit, declined.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.920
Used car prices were also becoming

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.870
too high for many buyers.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.940
Carvana said the average
price for their cars

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.420
increased by more than
30% from January 2021,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.067
to January 2022.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.800
And Carvana was dealing
with logistical problems

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.050
associated with the growth and demand.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.570
Complaints about the company were growing.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:53.010
- So Carvana customers started reporting

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:56.190
having issues with getting
the titles to their cars,

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.480
getting the paperwork in time,

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.430
being provided with
temporary license plates

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.590
from states that they didn't live in.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:04.020
And those stories became
more and more common

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.490
in the second half of last year.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.530
- [Narrator] In November,
Carvana said it was addressing

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.690
significant operational constraints,

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.020
due to its record growth and
labor shortages due to COVID.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:17.220
However, many of these issues
carried over into 2022.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:20.400
By May, Carvana's share price
hovered near a low point.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.140
The company announced
that it would lay off

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.880
roughly 12% of its workers,

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.970
after borrowing heavily to acquire Adesa.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.300
In July, Illinois moved to
suspend Carvana in the state

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.790
after complaints about
titles and registration.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.610
The state previously set strict
guidelines for the company

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.910
around issuing temporary
registration and license plates.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.580
Carvana was granted a
temporary restraining order

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.270
to continue selling cars in
the state at the end of July.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:47.857
Of the suspension, a
Carvana spokesperson said,

00:05:47.857 --> 00:05:50.880
"We provide title and
registration services at a rate

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.490
among the top performing
dealers in the state.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.800
Carvana shares of the state's
commitment to reducing

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.500
paperwork challenges as much as possible."

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.380
So where does Carvana go from here?

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.090
Quarter 2 earnings in August

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.850
showed an improvement
in retail unit sales.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.500
The company said it is focusing

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:10.350
on cutting costs and improving efficiency.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.570
It also said it expects
in the third quarter

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.180
to sell its loans to
financial institutions

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.580
instead of packaging them into securities.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.220
Its share price increased
by more than 40%,

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.290
the morning following the announcement.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.870
Carvana's path ahead may
depend on how it continues

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.760
to handle growth moving forward.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.330
- Well, when companies focus
so exclusively on growth,

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.500
they can, you know,

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.090
generate all sorts of
demand for their product

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.730
that they then, maybe
struggle to meet that demand.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.200
And then by the time they catch up,

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.240
you know the macro environment

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.860
and the demand for their
product for whatever reason,

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.600
whether it's used car prices

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.970
or supply chain issues or whatever,

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.740
all these kind of weird issues

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.180
that affected Carvana's business.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:52.740
They were overbuilt for what showed up.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.037
- [Narrator] A Carvana spokesperson said,

00:06:54.037 --> 00:06:56.730
"That the company remains
firmly committed to continuous

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.860
improvement and will
stay hard at work making

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.830
the best car buying and
selling experience available

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:02.760
even better."

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.350
Here's CEO, Ernie Garcia,

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.600
in a quarter 2 call to shareholders.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:07.680
- [Ernie Garcia] You're reducing the speed

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.520
at which we're growing today

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.260
given the shift in focus.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.480
But our hope and belief is
that by getting more efficient

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.970
it makes it easier to grow
faster in the future because,

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.620
you have kind of less work to do per sale.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.770
And so, you know, we'll hope
to get that back over time,

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.910
at some point.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.410
- [Narrator] The auto industry as a whole

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.960
has been impacted by
changing market conditions.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.720
But the share price for some
competitors, like CarMax,

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.380
have not been as severely
affected as Carvana.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.963
(gentle music)

